From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:50:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: add the ATC3 display crossbar

The T8132 has a display crossbar in the core window of each ATC; the J604
ADT lists atc3-dpxbar at 0x41b04c000 (0x4000) next to atc0/1/2-dpxbar,
and the J604 routes its third USB-C port through ATC3. Describe it,
disabled, in the form of the ATC0/1 crossbars.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index cf440c54e5..312b398fdd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -1053,6 +1053,18 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The ATC's display crossbar. Boards enable it with the external
+		 * display coprocessors whose Type-C routes use it.
+		 */
+		atc3_dpxbar: mux@41b04c000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8132-display-crossbar";
+			reg = <0x4 0x1b04c000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			#mux-control-cells = <1>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_atc3_usb>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		dwc3_3_dart_0: iommu@41af00000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8132-dart", "apple,t8110-dart";
 			reg = <0x4 0x1af00000 0x0 0xc000>;
